# Database Maintenance Runbook

## Overview
This document outlines procedures for maintaining the PostgreSQL database supporting the Security Audit Platform.

---

## Scheduled Maintenance Windows

| Day | Window | Duration | Tasks |
|-----|--------|----------|-------|
| Sunday | 02:00-04:00 UTC | 2 hours | Full vacuum, statistics update |
| Wednesday | 03:00-03:30 UTC | 30 min | Index rebuild (non-blocking) |
| Monthly | 1st Sunday 02:00 UTC | Variable | Full backup verification |

---

## Maintenance Procedures

### Vacuum & Statistics Update

```bash
# Run during maintenance window
sudo -u postgres psql -c "ANALYZE;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "VACUUM ANALYZE findings;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "VACUUM ANALYZE audit_cycles;"
```

### Index Rebuild (Non-blocking)

```sql
-- For PostgreSQL 12+, use CONCURRENTLY
REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_findings_severity;
REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_audit_timestamp;

-- For larger indexes, monitor progress
SELECT relname, indexrelname, pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size(indexrelid))
FROM pg_indexes
JOIN pg_class ON pg_class.oid = pg_indexes.indexrelid
WHERE schemaname = 'public';
```

### Connection Pool Tuning

```sql
-- Check current connections
SELECT count(*) FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE datname = 'security_audit';

-- Adjust max_connections if needed (requires restart)
ALTER SYSTEM SET max_connections = 200;
SELECT pg_reload_conf();
```

### Bloat Check

```sql
-- Check table bloat
SELECT 
    schemaname || '.' || relname AS table,
    pg_size_pretty(n_live_tup * avg_width) AS estimated_row_size,
    n_dead_tup AS dead_tuples,
    CASE 
        WHEN n_live_tup > 0 THEN round(100 * n_dead_tup / n_live_tup, 2)
        ELSE 0
    END AS dead_tuple_pct
FROM pg_stat_user_tables
ORDER BY n_dead_tup DESC;
```

### Partition Maintenance

```sql
-- For partitioned tables, detach old partitions
ALTER TABLE audit_cycles DETACH PARTITION audit_cycles_2023_01;

-- Archive to cold storage
INSERT INTO audit_cycles_archive SELECT * FROM audit_cycles_2023_01;
DROP TABLE audit_cycles_2023_01;
```

---

## Emergency Procedures

### Connection Exhaustion

```bash
# Find blocking queries
SELECT pid, usename, wait_event_type, state, query
FROM pg_stat_activity
WHERE state != 'idle'
ORDER BY state_change;

# Kill idle-in-transaction sessions
SELECT pg_terminate_backend(pid)
FROM pg_stat_activity
WHERE state = 'idle in transaction'
AND query_start < NOW() - INTERVAL '30 minutes';
```

### Replication Lag

```sql
-- Check replication lag
SELECT 
    application_name,
    state,
    pg_wal_lsn_diff(pg_current_wal_lsn(), replay_lsn)/1024/1024 AS lag_mb
FROM pg_stat_replication;

-- If lag > 100MB, investigate
-- Check disk I/O, network bandwidth
```

### Disk Space Emergency

```bash
# Quick space analysis
du -sh /var/lib/postgresql/*/base/* | sort -hr | head -10

# Vacuum large tables immediately
sudo -u postgres psql -c "VACUUM FULL audit_cycles;"

# Delete old backups (after verifying elsewhere)
find /var/lib/postgresql/backups -mtime +30 -delete
```

